-- Migration 285: restore the opening clause dropped from 92 RBI 2026 stems.
--
-- The 2026 loader merged each Directions block into every stem in its range
-- -- the right thing, and the reason RBI 2023-2025 have no orphans -- but
-- it dropped the first ~88 characters of every block it merged. 92 of the
-- paper's 191 questions therefore begin mid-sentence. 89 are verified and
-- live.
--
-- Q190 reads "numbered I and II given below it. You have to decide whether
-- the data provided in the statements are sufficient to answer the
-- question." The source reads "Directions (190 -193) - Each of the
-- following consists of a question and two statements numbered I and II
-- given below it. ...". Everything before "numbered" was lost. This
-- restores it, per row, from docs/reference/pyq/RBI-
-- Grade-B-2026-Phase-1-Previous-Year-Papers-Book.pdf.
--
-- IT IS A FIXED-WIDTH CUT, which is the strongest evidence for what
-- happened: across all 92 rows the restored head is between 84 and 92
-- characters, clustered on 88 (32 rows) and 87 (18). Not a parse that lost
-- a sentence here and there -- a loader that sliced a constant number of
-- characters off the front.
-- head length: 84ch x5, 85ch x5, 86ch x3, 87ch x18, 88ch x32, 89ch x13, 90ch x8, 91ch x2, 92ch x6
--
-- HOW EACH HEAD WAS FOUND. For every truncated stem: take the Directions
-- block covering its number, reduce both the block and the stem to
-- lowercase alphanumerics (so that spacing, hyphenation and injected page
-- furniture cannot break the match), find the longest anchor of 12-40
-- characters from the stem's opening that occurs exactly once in the block,
-- and cut the block there. The anchor must be unique or the row is refused.
-- The relaxed comparison is what makes this work: the loaded text writes
-- "odd-numbered" where the source prints "odd - numbered", and the source
-- carries "50 RBI Grade B 2026 Phase 1 Recollected Questions" in the middle
-- of one setup.
--
-- All 92 reconstruct. Every restored head appears verbatim in the source
-- and every one begins "Direction(s) (". Nothing is invented; no stem text
-- is altered, only prefixed.
