   'Directions (168-173): Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below. Eight persons, namely A, B, C, D, E, F, G and H, are sitting around a circular table facing the centre, but not necessarily in the same order. Each person likes a different natural place among Lake, River, Mountain, Forest, Desert, Valley, Island and Beach. The number of persons sitting between F and C is the same as the number of persons sitting between the one who likes Beach and E. The one who likes Lake sits opposite the one who likes Beach. F sits second to the left of the one who likes Beach. B sits immediately to the left of the one who likes River. The one who likes Mountain sits immediately to the right of the one who likes River. Only one person sits between B and the one who likes Island. C sits immediately to the left of the one who likes Island. G sits immediately to the right of the one who likes Beach. The one who likes Desert sits second to the right of the one who likes Island. The one who likes Valley sits immediately to the right of the one who likes Beach. A sits immediately between the one who likes Mountain and the one who likes Valley. H sits adjacent to the one who likes Forest. The number of persons sitting between the one who likes Beach and the one who likes Island, when counted from the right of the one who likes Beach, is the same as the number of persons sitting between which of the following pairs, when counted from the right of the first person?'),
  ('129ec5c5-a22f-4c69-ba11-33eb0f22db3e'::uuid,
   'Directions (168-173): Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below. Eight persons, namely A, B, C, D, E, F, G and H, are sitting around a circular table facing the centre, but not necessarily in the same order. Each person likes a different natural place among Lake, River, Mountain, Forest, Desert, Valley, Island and Beach. The number of persons sitting between F and C is the same as the number of persons sitting between the one who likes Beach and E. The one who likes Lake sits opposite the one who likes Beach. F sits second to the left of the one who likes Beach. B sits immediately to the left of the one who likes River. The one who likes Mountain sits immediately to the right of the one who likes River. Only one person sits between B and the one who likes Island. C sits immediately to the left of the one who likes Island. G sits immediately to the right of the one who likes Beach. The one who likes Desert sits second to the right of the one who likes Island. The one who likes Valley sits immediately to the right of the one who likes Beach. A sits immediately between the one who likes Mountain and the one who likes Valley. H sits adjacent to the one who likes Forest. If the one who likes River is related to the one who likes Valley and the one who likes Desert is related to the one who likes Beach in the same manner, then the one who likes Lake is related to which of the following?'),
  ('a3302c7e-72a4-430c-9583-79e2b7211d0b'::uuid,
   'Directions (174 -178) Study the following information carefully and answer the below questions. The numbers arrangement machine when given an input line of numbers rearranges them following a particular rule in each step. The following is an illustration of input and rearrangement. Input: 245 368 127 492 583 716 639 854 431 Step I: 644 245 127 492 583 716 854 431 365 Step II: 588 644 245 127 716 854 431 365 489 Step III: 436 588 644 245 127 854 365 489 713 Step IV: 250 436 588 644 127 365 489 713 851 Step V: 132 250 436 588 644 365 489 713 851 Step V is the last step Input: 537 684 219 456 795 328 671 942 153 What is the sum of the number which is 3rd from the left end in Step III and the number which is 4th from the right end in Step V?'),
  ('19e983b0-cba0-4bcd-ba7b-ee8930eb5b50'::uuid,
   'Directions (174 -178) Study the following information carefully and answer the below questions. The numbers arrangement machine when given an input line of numbers rearranges them following a particular rule in each step. The following is an illustration of input and rearrangement. Input: 245 368 127 492 583 716 639 854 431 Step I: 644 245 127 492 583 716 854 431 365 Step II: 588 644 245 127 716 854 431 365 489 Step III: 436 588 644 245 127 854 365 489 713 Step IV: 250 436 588 644 127 365 489 713 851 Step V: 132 250 436 588 644 365 489 713 851 Step V is the last step Input: 537 684 219 456 795 328 671 942 153 In Step IV, how many numbers are there between the number obtained from 671 and the number obtained from 942?'),
  ('aa01d948-d961-496f-9669-77329925f156'::uuid,
   'Directions (174 -178) Study the following information carefully and answer the below questions. The numbers arrangement machine when given an input line of numbers rearranges them following a particular rule in each step. The following is an illustration of input and rearrangement. Input: 245 368 127 492 583 716 639 854 431 Step I: 644 245 127 492 583 716 854 431 365 Step II: 588 644 245 127 716 854 431 365 489 Step III: 436 588 644 245 127 854 365 489 713 Step IV: 250 436 588 644 127 365 489 713 851 Step V: 132 250 436 588 644 365 489 713 851 Step V is the last step Input: 537 684 219 456 795 328 671 942 153 Which of the following statements is/are true? I. In Step III, only two numbers are between 219 and 325. II. In Step V, 158 is placed immediately to the right of 224. III. In Step II, 453 is placed at the extreme right end.'),
  ('f53fcb36-0c16-45e6-a5b3-b4a176e09f4e'::uuid,
   'Directions (174 -178) Study the following information carefully and answer the below questions. The numbers arrangement machine when given an input line of numbers rearranges them following a particular rule in each step. The following is an illustration of input and rearrangement. Input: 245 368 127 492 583 716 639 854 431 Step I: 644 245 127 492 583 716 854 431 365 Step II: 588 644 245 127 716 854 431 365 489 Step III: 436 588 644 245 127 854 365 489 713 Step IV: 250 436 588 644 127 365 489 713 851 Step V: 132 250 436 588 644 365 489 713 851 Step V is the last step Input: 537 684 219 456 795 328 671 942 153 Which of the following step is correctly represents step III?'),
  ('a5f6375e-9e7f-4def-930d-7209b932f699'::uuid,
   'Directions (174 -178) Study the following information carefully and answer the below questions. The numbers arrangement machine when given an input line of numbers rearranges them following a particular rule in each step. The following is an illustration of input and rearrangement. Input: 245 368 127 492 583 716 639 854 431 Step I: 644 245 127 492 583 716 854 431 365 Step II: 588 644 245 127 716 854 431 365 489 Step III: 436 588 644 245 127 854 365 489 713 Step IV: 250 436 588 644 127 365 489 713 851 Step V: 132 250 436 588 644 365 489 713 851 Step V is the last step Input: 537 684 219 456 795 328 671 942 153 In which of the following steps are the three numbers “684 219 942” found in the same sequence?'),
  ('f7041059-6753-430f-9c82-e616348dd919'::uuid,
   'Directions (182-186) Study the following information carefully and answer the questions below. A certain number of persons are sitting in a row. All of them are facing the north. Each of them likes different chocolates. Q is sitting fourth to the right of P. The number of persons sitting between M and Q is equal to the number of persons sitting between Q and G. Q is sitting second to the left of W. Five people are sitting between W and F, who likes Milky Bar. One person is sitting between F and D. Three people are sitting between D and R. The number of persons sitting between Q and F is equal to the number of persons sitting between F and the person sitting at the extreme right end. Z is the second person from one of the extreme ends. Nine people are sitting between Z and E, who like 5-star. The person who likes Dairy milk is sitting ninth from one of the extreme ends. Three people are sitting to the left of M. One person is sitting between M and the person who likes KitKat. Three people are sitting between P and the person who likes KitKat. How many people are sitting in the row?'),
  ('270ea394-1681-4a13-bea8-d2b174564177'::uuid,
   'Directions (182-186) Study the following information carefully and answer the questions below. A certain number of persons are sitting in a row. All of them are facing the north. Each of them likes different chocolates. Q is sitting fourth to the right of P. The number of persons sitting between M and Q is equal to the number of persons sitting between Q and G. Q is sitting second to the left of W. Five people are sitting between W and F, who likes Milky Bar. One person is sitting between F and D. Three people are sitting between D and R. The number of persons sitting between Q and F is equal to the number of persons sitting between F and the person sitting at the extreme right end. Z is the second person from one of the extreme ends. Nine people are sitting between Z and E, who like 5-star. The person who likes Dairy milk is sitting ninth from one of the extreme ends. Three people are sitting to the left of M. One person is sitting between M and the person who likes KitKat. Three people are sitting between P and the person who likes KitKat. What is the position of P with respect to the one who likes Dairy Milk?'),
  ('83f93856-1b28-4937-be40-545dc6053336'::uuid,
   'Directions (182-186) Study the following information carefully and answer the questions below. A certain number of persons are sitting in a row. All of them are facing the north. Each of them likes different chocolates. Q is sitting fourth to the right of P. The number of persons sitting between M and Q is equal to the number of persons sitting between Q and G. Q is sitting second to the left of W. Five people are sitting between W and F, who likes Milky Bar. One person is sitting between F and D. Three people are sitting between D and R. The number of persons sitting between Q and F is equal to the number of persons sitting between F and the person sitting at the extreme right end. Z is the second person from one of the extreme ends. Nine people are sitting between Z and E, who like 5-star. The person who likes Dairy milk is sitting ninth from one of the extreme ends. Three people are sitting to the left of M. One person is sitting between M and the person who likes KitKat. Three people are sitting between P and the person who likes KitKat. Who among the following persons sits fourth to the left of the one who sits second to the right of F?'),
  ('541d5b75-80a7-4b6e-abd2-06a9d03ced3a'::uuid,
   'Directions (182-186) Study the following information carefully and answer the questions below. A certain number of persons are sitting in a row. All of them are facing the north. Each of them likes different chocolates. Q is sitting fourth to the right of P. The number of persons sitting between M and Q is equal to the number of persons sitting between Q and G. Q is sitting second to the left of W. Five people are sitting between W and F, who likes Milky Bar. One person is sitting between F and D. Three people are sitting between D and R. The number of persons sitting between Q and F is equal to the number of persons sitting between F and the person sitting at the extreme right end. Z is the second person from one of the extreme ends. Nine people are sitting between Z and E, who like 5-star. The person who likes Dairy milk is sitting ninth from one of the extreme ends. Three people are sitting to the left of M. One person is sitting between M and the person who likes KitKat. Three people are sitting between P and the person who likes KitKat. If P is related to the one who likes Dairy Milk, in the same way W is related to the one who likes 5-star, then who among the following persons is related to the one who likes Milky Bar?'),
  ('84280078-7db8-4595-b98e-109a95a61c2b'::uuid,
   'Directions (182-186) Study the following information carefully and answer the questions below. A certain number of persons are sitting in a row. All of them are facing the north. Each of them likes different chocolates. Q is sitting fourth to the right of P. The number of persons sitting between M and Q is equal to the number of persons sitting between Q and G. Q is sitting second to the left of W. Five people are sitting between W and F, who likes Milky Bar. One person is sitting between F and D. Three people are sitting between D and R. The number of persons sitting between Q and F is equal to the number of persons sitting between F and the person sitting at the extreme right end. Z is the second person from one of the extreme ends. Nine people are sitting between Z and E, who like 5-star. The person who likes Dairy milk is sitting ninth from one of the extreme ends. Three people are sitting to the left of M. One person is sitting between M and the person who likes KitKat. Three people are sitting between P and the person who likes KitKat. Which of the following statements is/are true with respect to the final arrangement?'),
  ('6021fdea-040b-4457-9b43-fd3e7612cbf2'::uuid,
   'Directions (187-189) In each of the following questions, a statement is followed by three assumptions numbered I, II and III. An assumption is something supposed or taken for granted. Read the statement carefully and decide which of the given assumptions is/are implicit in the statement. Statement: The bank has advised customers to update their mobile numbers and email IDs in their accounts. This will help them receive transaction alerts, security messages and important account-related updates on time. Assumptions: I. Some customers may not have updated their latest contact details with the bank. II. Customers who update their contact details will get higher interest on deposits. III. Timely alerts can help customers remain informed about account activities. Which of the above assumptions is/are implicit? Only III'),
  ('0d0b8894-ba2c-40eb-aaa1-35f80c5f2635'::uuid,
   'Directions (187-189) In each of the following questions, a statement is followed by three assumptions numbered I, II and III. An assumption is something supposed or taken for granted. Read the statement carefully and decide which of the given assumptions is/are implicit in the statement. Statement: The state government has launched a mobile app to help citizens register complaints related to damaged roads, poor street lighting and garbage collection. The complaints will be forwarded directly to the concerned local department. Officials have been instructed to update the complaint status within a fixed time limit. Assumptions: I. Citizens may face civic issues that need timely attention from local departments. II. A mobile app can help in faster reporting and tracking of public complaints. III. All complaints received through the app will be solved immediately. Which of the above assumptions is/are implicit?'),
  ('3dc341c2-c286-47d2-ba29-00a1fd23b9f8'::uuid,
   'Directions (187-189) In each of the following questions, a statement is followed by three assumptions numbered I, II and III. An assumption is something supposed or taken for granted. Read the statement carefully and decide which of the given assumptions is/are implicit in the statement. Statement: A hospital has started an online appointment system to reduce crowding at the registration counter. Patients can book their preferred time slot through the hospital website or mobile app. The hospital has also kept a separate help desk for patients who are unable to use the online system. Assumptions: I. Online appointments can help in reducing crowding at the hospital registration counter. II. Some patients may not be comfortable using the online appointment system. III. Patients booking appointments online will receive free medical consultation. Which of the above assumptions is/are implicit?'),
  ('830874ab-c231-4e31-9078-a768a8d98229'::uuid,
   'Directions (190 -193) - Each of the following consists of a question and two statements numbered I and II given below it. You have to decide whether the data provided in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Seven persons – A, B, C, D, E, F, and G are sitting in a row facing north but not necessarily in the same order. How many persons are sitting between C and E? Statement I. C sits on either end. Two persons are sitting between C and G. The person sitting adjacent to G sits fourth to the right of A, who neither sits adjacent to E nor D. Statement II. F sits third to the left of B, who sits third from the end. Two persons are sitting between D and E, who doesn’t sit at the end. C sits third to the right of G, who doesn’t sit adjacent to F.'),
  ('67849f20-0f5f-492e-a04d-b3cd13ee4194'::uuid,
   'Directions (190 -193) - Each of the following consists of a question and two statements numbered I and II given below it. You have to decide whether the data provided in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. What is the code for “fresh fruit”? Statement I: “fresh sweet fruit” is coded as “ka la mi” and “sweet juice fruit” is coded as “la mi pa”. Statement II: “fruit green basket” is coded as “mi ro ta” and “fresh green mango” is coded as “ka ro se”.'),
  ('d66dbd25-193f-40a9-b4c2-67faaa70f4ec'::uuid,
   'Directions (190 -193) - Each of the following consists of a question and two statements numbered I and II given below it. You have to decide whether the data provided in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Six persons P, Q, R, S, T and U went to Delhi on six different days of the same week starting from Monday to Saturday. Who went to Delhi on Wednesday? Statement I: Q went immediately before R. Only one person went between R and T. P went immediately after T. S went before Q. U went after R but before T. Statement II: P went immediately after U. Only one person went between Q and T. S went before Q. R went after T but not on Saturday.'),
  ('c27d47bb-e1c5-4220-85ec-b3c6a64c04ee'::uuid,
   'Directions (190 -193) - Each of the following consists of a question and two statements numbered I and II given below it. You have to decide whether the data provided in the statements are sufficient to answer the question. Six persons A, B, C, D, E and F hold six different designations in a company, namely Chairman, Managing Director, General Manager, Senior Manager, Assistant Manager and Executive. The designations are given in decreasing order of seniority from Chairman to Executive. Who among the following is the General Manager? Statement I: A is senior to B. C is junior to F. Only one person is between D and E in designation order. B is not the Chairman. Statement II: B is senior to D but junior to A. Only one person is senior to A. E is immediately junior to D. F is senior to C. E is not junior to C.'),
  ('074dc60b-1db5-46e4-bea0-c6c6048bb00a'::uuid,
   'Directions (194 -195) - Read the following paragraph carefully and answer the questions given below. Paragraph: A smartwatch company recently marketed its new smartwatch as a reliable and high- performance product. However, soon after launch, many customers posted negative reviews regarding delayed syncing, inaccurate health readings and sudden device shutdowns. The CEO responded that the complaints were mainly due to a temporary server issue and not because of any defect in the watch. Later, an independent technology analyst reviewed the product and stated that both server instability and hardware-related faults were affecting the smartwatch’s performance. Which of the following should be the most appropriate course of action for the smartwatch company?'),
  ('c7110f95-ad59-4b73-9d7a-03b4855cabd8'::uuid,
   'Directions (194 -195) - Read the following paragraph carefully and answer the questions given below. Paragraph: A smartwatch company recently marketed its new smartwatch as a reliable and high- performance product. However, soon after launch, many customers posted negative reviews regarding delayed syncing, inaccurate health readings and sudden device shutdowns. The CEO responded that the complaints were mainly due to a temporary server issue and not because of any defect in the watch. Later, an independent technology analyst reviewed the product and stated that both server instability and hardware-related faults were affecting the smartwatch’s performance. Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the CEO’s statement?'),
  ('64e82d39-e2f4-4a61-9bfd-205aea9da93e'::uuid,
   'Directions (196-197) - In each of the following questions, a statement is followed by three inferences numbered I, II and III. Read the statement carefully and decide which of the given inferences logically follows from the information given in the statement. Statement: Several cities have issued heatwave alerts as temperatures remain unusually high for many days. Hospitals have reported more cases of dehydration and heat exhaustion, especially among elderly people and outdoor workers. Local authorities have advised citizens to avoid direct sunlight during afternoon hours and drink enough water. Inferences: I. All citizens will follow the advisory issued by local authorities. II. Heatwaves can create health risks for vulnerable groups. III. Outdoor workers may be more exposed to heat-related illness than people working indoors.'),
  ('07106371-ba56-4cbc-8ecb-8f861edd7eba'::uuid,
   'Directions (196-197) - In each of the following questions, a statement is followed by three inferences numbered I, II and III. Read the statement carefully and decide which of the given inferences logically follows from the information given in the statement. Statement: During the Iran-US war, global markets reacted sharply due to fears of disruption in oil supply routes. Several countries appealed for restraint and asked both sides to return to diplomatic talks. Humanitarian agencies also warned that prolonged conflict could affect civilians and regional stability. Inferences: I. The conflict may have an impact beyond the two countries directly involved. II. Diplomatic talks are being viewed as a possible way to reduce tensions. III. The war has already ended because several countries appealed for restraint. Which of the above inferences logically follows?'),
  ('19e4483c-2e5b-4b70-a7ba-2e24294fe08c'::uuid,
   'Directions (198) - Read the following statement carefully and choose the conclusion that logically follows from the information given in the statement. Statement: The Reserve Bank of India’s Clean Note Policy aims to ensure that the public receives clean and good-quality currency notes. Banks are expected to sort notes into issuable and non- issuable categories and avoid practices such as stapling or writing on currency notes. Soiled or unfit notes are to be withdrawn from circulation through the banking system. Which of the following conclusions can be drawn from the above statement?'),
  ('7ee89048-57e0-4e8e-b5c4-0c671d43c100'::uuid,
   'Directions (199) - Read the following statement carefully and identify the most possible reason behind the situation described. Situation: Several customers have complained that their debit card transactions failed even though sufficient balance was available in their accounts. The bank later informed customers that the issue occurred only for a short period and was limited to a few payment channels. The bank also stated that failed transaction amounts, if debited, would be reversed automatically. Which of the following is the most possible reason for the failed transactions?'),
  ('9516e964-0c16-4820-b5f6-c1d888688ba8'::uuid,
   'Directions (200) - Read the given situation carefully and choose the statement that best supports or strengthens it. Situation: A leading e-commerce company has introduced a same-day delivery service in selected metro cities. The company stated that this service is being launched to meet growing customer demand for faster delivery and to improve customer satisfaction. Which of the following statements supports the given situation?')
) AS v(question_id, question_text)
WHERE q.id = v.question_id
  AND q.question_text IS DISTINCT FROM v.question_text;

